From f072bd0b025d7ebc9db647aa05038a54a425882f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:21:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] ppc-darwin: gate the thread-QoS switch on the
 deployment target

Hygiene for patch 0038, folded into the full rebuild that the harness's
node-feature change forces anyway.  0038 compiled platform-posix.cc's
QoS switch out with `defined(QOS_CLASS_BACKGROUND)`, but sys/qos.h
declares the QOS_CLASS_* values as enum members, not macros, so that
test is false on every SDK: correct by accident on the PowerPC targets,
where it is what we want, but a >= 10.10 build of the patched tree lost
its thread QoS.  Test the deployment target instead, with the compiler's
__ENVIRONMENT_MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED__ (always defined on Darwin,
no <AvailabilityMacros.h> include and no min-vs-max #error hazard).
Identical object code on the PowerPC targets.
---
 v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc b/v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
index fe19fea..6a98cee 100644
--- a/v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
+++ b/v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
@@ -1184,8 +1184,10 @@ static void* ThreadEntry(void* arg) {
   SetThreadName(thread->name());
 // The QoS API appeared in 10.10; on the PowerPC-era SDKs the priority stays
 // an unapplied hint (there is no per-thread setpriority on Darwin, and the
-// scheduler works fine without it).
-#if V8_OS_DARWIN && defined(QOS_CLASS_BACKGROUND)
+// scheduler works fine without it).  Gate on the deployment target: the
+// QOS_CLASS_* values are enum members, not macros, so defined() cannot see
+// them, and the compiler always provides this macro on Darwin.
+#if V8_OS_DARWIN && (__ENVIRONMENT_MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED__ >= 101000)
   switch (thread->priority()) {
     case Thread::Priority::kBestEffort:
       pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_BACKGROUND, 0);
-- 
